# will_lesson_object — a will wants the object that taught it
#
# Examining petroglyphs teaches archeology, and archeology is a will: to dig old ground, to study a
# relic, to fetch a spade. Carvings in rock are none of those, so the mind the carvings taught used to
# refuse them — picked to think on the petroglyphs, it said it had no interest and only leaving would
# serve. Its targets now end on WillTarget.Teaching<ArcheologyModusMentis>(): whatever declares
# archeology its own lesson. From the Dry Wash the petroglyphs are right there, one step.
# --will-lesson-audit is the check over every object and every will; this is the case that was reported.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --grant-mm archeology --location-type canyon --location-id 1 --start-area "Dry Wash" --period morning

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60
advance 12 180

expect-state will "will archeology steps=1"
expect-state will "petroglyphs"
quit
